# Silead touch calibration [V] 2026-10-26: taps at the screen's top-left, top-right and bottom-left
# read (2%, 97%), (98%, 96%), (2%, 4%) on the device, so x is right and y is flipped. cog's drm
# platform does not rotate touch (libinput rotation is pointer-only); it scales the calibrated
# point onto the rotated screen, so this matrix is all the mapping there is.
ACTION=="add|change", SUBSYSTEM=="input", ATTRS{name}=="silead_ts", ENV{LIBINPUT_CALIBRATION_MATRIX}="1 0 0 0 -1 1"
